Sending keys: ["cat <<'EOF' > /app/vuln-report.md\n# Vulnerability Report: Entry Vector Analysis\n\n## 1. Confirmed Exploited Vulnerability\n- **CVE ID:** `CVE-2024-23897` (cited at `/sas/vulns.json:3`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:17`)\n- **Component:** Jenkins Controller (CLI Command Parser)\n- **Severity:** CVSS 9.8 (Critical) v3.1 (CWE-22 / CWE-27)\n- **Affected Versions:** Jenkins 2.441 and earlier, LTS 2.426.2 and earlier\n- **Vulnerability Description:** Jenkins CLI uses args4j parser, which expands `@` followed by a file path into file contents. This allows unauthenticated attackers to read arbitrary files on the Jenkins controller file system or achieve Remote Code Execution (RCE) via serialized payload deserialization.\n\n## 2. Exploitation Analysis & Forensic Proof\n- **Entry Artifact:** `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/jobs/.tmp/config.xml:3`\n- **Artifact Analysis:** The file `/var/lib/jenkins/jobs/.tmp/config.xml` contains deserialization payload evidence (`Jenkins CLI RCE artifact via an @type deserialization gadget`), confirming that the attacker leveraged CVE-2024-23897 to drop configurations/code into the Jenkins environment.\n- **Authentication State:** The Jenkins controller had security features disabled (`useSecurity=false` in `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/config.xml:3`), allowing anonymous unauthenticated administrative access and making exploitation trivial.\n\n## 3. Explicit Rejection of Non-Applicable CVEs\n- **CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep):** Erroneously listed in initial shift notes (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:10`).\n- **Rejection Reason:** CVE-2019-0708 is a Remote Code Execution vulnerability in Microsoft Remote Desktop Services (RDP) on Windows systems. The target host (`jenkins-prod-01`) is an Ubuntu 22.04 Linux host running a Jenkins controller on Java/Nginx (`/disk/etc/os-release`, `/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log`). BlueKeep is completely inapplicable to Linux and RDP is not running on this host.\n\n## 4. Vulnerability Remediation\n- Upgrade Jenkins core to version 2.442 / LTS 2.426.3 or higher.\n- Disable CLI access or set Java system property `-Djenkins.CLI.disabled=true` as an immediate workaround prior to patching.\n- Re-enable authentication and security realm (`useSecurity=true`) in `/var/lib/jenkins/config.xml`.\nEOF\n"] min_timeout_sec: 0.5 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
