Sending keys: ["cat << 'EOF' > /app/vuln-report.md\n# Vulnerability Assessment & Initial Entry Analysis Report\n\n## Executive Summary\nThis report analyzes the entry vector utilized during the compromise of `log4shell-prod-01`. The primary vulnerability exploited was **Log4Shell (`CVE-2021-44228`)**, an critical Remote Code Execution (RCE) vulnerability present in Apache Log4j2 versions 2.0-beta9 through 2.15.0.\n\nThe draft change ticket (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:8`) mistakenly referenced `CVE-2019-0708` (BlueKeep, a Windows Remote Desktop Protocol vulnerability). Forensic analysis confirms BlueKeep is completely irrelevant to this Ubuntu Linux system and was **not** the initial access vector.\n\n## Vulnerability Analysis: CVE-2021-44228 (Log4Shell)\n- **Vulnerability Identifier**: CVE-2021-44228 (`/sas/vulns.json:4`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:19-21`).\n- **CVSS Score**: 10.0 (Critical) (v3.1) (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:19`).\n- **CWE Classification**: CWE-20, CWE-400, CWE-502, CWE-917 (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:19`).\n- **Affected Component**: Apache Log4j2 library version 2.14 (`/disk/opt/app/log4j2.xml:3`).\n\n### Exploitation Mechanics\n1. **Configuration Vulnerability (`BAS-01` / `CHK-06`)**:\n   - The application configuration file at `/disk/opt/app/log4j2.xml:1-4` had message-lookup JNDI functionality enabled (`/disk/opt/app/log4j2.xml:3`, also cited in `/sas/alerts.json:27-32` and `/sas/baseline.json:3-6`).\n2. **JNDI Injection Protocol**:\n   - The remote adversary transmitted an HTTP request containing a JNDI LDAP lookup payload string (`${jndi:ldap://...}`) as documented in `/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp:2` and `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:11,20`.\n3. **Payload Execution & Web Shell Dropper**:\n   - Upon processing the malicious log string, Log4j2 queried the remote LDAP server controlled by the attacker (`198.51.100.136` cited in `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5,24`), deserialized the remote object, and executed arbitrary code.\n   - This execution dropped the initial JSP web shell at `/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp:1-2` (`ALERT-01` in `/sas/alerts.json:3-8`).\n\n## Refutation of Erroneous Vulnerability Claims\n- **Claim in Draft Ticket**: Row 2 of `/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:8` proposes patching `CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep)` on RDP.\n- **Forensic Refutation**:\n  1. System identity is Ubuntu 22.04 LTS (`/disk/etc/os-release`). BlueKeep (`CVE-2019-0708`) specifically targets Microsoft Windows RDP protocol (`termdd.sys`).\n  2. RDP service is not installed or exposed on this host.\n  3. All initial access log signatures, web application requests, and artifacts point exclusively to Log4j2 JNDI exploitation (`/disk/opt/app/log4j2.xml:3`, `/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp:2`, `/sas/vulns.json:4`).\n  4. Conclusion: Row 2 of `/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:8` is invalid and must be replaced with Log4j2 remediation / upgrade (`CVE-2021-44228`).\n\n## Remediation Requirements\n1. Upgrade Apache Log4j2 to version `2.17.1` or later (or `2.15.0`+ with message lookups disabled).\n2. Update web application configuration (`/disk/opt/app/log4j2.xml:1-4`) to ensure `log4j2.formatMsgNoLookups=true` is set.\nEOF\n"] min_timeout_sec: 1.0 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
