Sending keys: ["cat << 'EOF' > /app/baseline-report.md\n# Baseline Configuration & Security Control Audit Report\n\n## Executive Summary\nThis report details baseline configuration weaknesses, system hardening failures, and security monitoring gaps identified during the investigation of `log4shell-prod-01`.\n\nThe baseline check `BAS-01` (`/sas/baseline.json:3-6`) identified a critical application configuration defect in `/disk/opt/app/log4j2.xml:1-4`. Furthermore, systemic OS-level hardening gaps permitted arbitrary file drops, cron persistence installation, and systemd service creation without triggering EDR or baseline integrity alerts.\n\n## Configuration & Hardening Deficiencies\n\n### 1. Insecure Application Logging Configuration (`BAS-01` / `CHK-06`)\n- **Location**: `/disk/opt/app/log4j2.xml:1-4` (cited in `/sas/baseline.json:3-6` and `/sas/alerts.json:27-32`).\n- **Defect**: Log4j2 configuration permitted message lookup interpolations with remote JNDI evaluation enabled (`/disk/opt/app/log4j2.xml:3`).\n- **Impact**: Allowed untrusted user inputs in HTTP headers and request parameters to trigger remote LDAP lookups (`${jndi:ldap://...}`) and achieve unauthenticated RCE (`/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp:2`).\n\n### 2. Excessive Web Directory Write Permissions\n- **Location**: `/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/`\n- **Defect**: The web server process owned or had full write privileges on static web application subdirectories.\n- **Impact**: Enabled the attacker to write both the primary JSP web shell (`/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp:1-2`) and the hidden secondary backup shell (`/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/.helper.jsp:1-2`).\n- **Hardening Mandate**: Static web directories should be mounted read-only or restricted to prevent dynamic file creation by application runtime service accounts.\n\n### 3. Execution Rights & Absence of `noexec` on `/tmp`\n- **Location**: `/disk/tmp/.sysd:1-2`\n- **Defect**: The `/tmp` filesystem allowed binary and shell script execution.\n- **Impact**: Allowed the attacker to drop and execute the reverse shell beacon binary/script at `/disk/tmp/.sysd:1-2` (`ALERT-02` in `/sas/alerts.json:10-17`).\n- **Hardening Mandate**: `/tmp` and `/var/tmp` must be mounted with `noexec,nosuid,nodev` options in `/disk/etc/fstab`.\n\n### 4. System Integrity Monitoring & Cron / Systemd Gaps\n- **Locations**:\n  - System Cron Directory: `/disk/etc/cron.d/apache-cache:1-5`\n  - Systemd Service Directory: `/disk/etc/systemd/system/apache-cache.service:1-7`\n- **Defect**: Absence of File Integrity Monitoring (FIM) or write restrictions on critical system configuration directories `/etc/cron.d/` and `/etc/systemd/system/`.\n- **Impact**: Unprivileged or escalated processes successfully established dual persistence mechanisms disguised under pseudo-legitimate names (`apache-cache`).\n\n## Security Detection & Telemetry Coverage Gaps\n\nA comparison between on-disk evidence and the automated security monitoring feed (`/sas/alerts.json:1-34`) highlights severe detection omissions:\n\n1. **Silent Cron Persistence Omission (`CHK-03`)**:\n   - The active cron file at `/disk/etc/cron.d/apache-cache:1-5` was **not detected** by security scans, allowing automated re-infection beacons (`/disk/etc/cron.d/apache-cache:5`) to operate silently.\n2. **Silent Secondary Web Shell Omission (`CHK-05`)**:\n   - The dot-prefixed backup web shell at `/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/.helper.jsp:1-2` bypassed static directory web shell detection.\n3. **Anti-Forensic Wiped Artifacts Omission**:\n   - Attacker wiping operations left residual recovered data in `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` without generating anti-forensics / log erasure alerts.\n\n## Baseline Hardening Recommendations\n- Implement File Integrity Monitoring (FIM) covering `/etc/cron.*`, `/etc/systemd/system/`, and web root static directories.\n- Mount `/tmp` with `noexec` options.\n- Restrict file permissions across `/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/` so application user `tomcat` cannot modify application code or static assets.\nEOF\n"] min_timeout_sec: 1.0 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
