Sending keys: ["cat <<'EOF' > /app/remediation-plan.md\n# Remediation and Response Plan\n\n## Overview\nThis plan outlines prioritized, step-by-step technical remediation instructions for host `postgres-prod-01`. All recommendations adhere to the containment principle of preferring backup and quarantine over destructive deletion. Every action directly addresses findings verified on `/disk` and reconciles change ticket `CHG-6386` (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md`).\n\n---\n\n## Reconciled Change Ticket: CHG-6386\nBelow is the reconciled change ticket table reflecting verified findings from `/disk` and `/sas`:\n\n| # | Action | Target | Status | Note / Evidence Citation |\n|---|--------|--------|--------|--------------------------|\n| 1 | Block malicious source IP inbound & outbound | `198.51.100.214` | Proposed | Corrected IP from stale `203.0.113.9` to `198.51.100.214` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6`, `/disk/var/spool/cron/postgres:5`, `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`). |\n| 2 | Harden PostgreSQL auth & revoke program execution | `/var/lib/pgsql/data/pg_hba.conf` | Proposed | Replaced irrelevant BlueKeep CVE-2019-0708 with database authentication hardening. Remove `trust` auth for `0.0.0.0/0` (`/disk/var/lib/pgsql/data/pg_hba.conf:3`). |\n| 3 | Remove & quarantine malicious cron job | `/var/spool/cron/postgres` | Proposed | Corrected path from `/var/spool/cron/root` to `/var/spool/cron/postgres` (`/disk/var/spool/cron/postgres:5`). Downgraded status from DONE to Proposed (unverified entry was still active on disk). |\n| 4 | Quarantine dropped malware binary | `/var/lib/pgsql/.local/pgdaemon` | Proposed | Silent artifact added. Quarantine dropper binary (`/disk/var/lib/pgsql/.local/pgdaemon`, SHA256: `c7e7e38fa8ffb3ba9b679b14d14ba7196d89d0c691c53f6bac576dee284cd603`). |\n| 5 | Disable & quarantine malicious systemd service | `/etc/systemd/system/pg-metrics.service` | Proposed | Silent artifact added. Disable and quarantine malicious systemd service (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/pg-metrics.service:5`). Maintain benign `/etc/systemd/system/pg-backup.service` (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/pg-backup.service:3`). |\n| 6 | Remove & quarantine DNS tunnel configuration | `/etc/pgdaemon.conf` | Proposed | Silent artifact added. Quarantine DNS tunnel C2 configuration (`/disk/etc/pgdaemon.conf:3`). |\n| 7 | Quarantine timestomping forensic artifacts | `/var/lib/pgsql/.local/.timestamps` | Proposed | Silent artifact added. Preserve and quarantine timestomping log file (`/disk/var/lib/pgsql/.local/.timestamps:2`). |\n\n---\n\n## Prioritized Execution Steps\n\n### Phase 1: Containment & Isolation (Immediate)\n1. **Network Layer Containment**\n   - Action: Block inbound and outbound traffic to attacker IP `198.51.100.214` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6`).\n   - Command: `iptables -A INPUT -s 198.51.100.214 -j DROP && iptables -A OUTPUT -d 198.51.100.214 -j DROP`\n   - Verification: `iptables -L -n -v | grep 198.51.100.214`\n\n2. **Block C2 DNS Resolver**\n   - Action: Sinkhole / drop DNS queries targeting `update-postgres.example.cn` (`/disk/etc/pgdaemon.conf:3`, `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`).\n   - Command: Add `0.0.0.0 update-postgres.example.cn` to `/etc/hosts`.\n   - Verification: `ping -c 1 update-postgres.example.cn` resolves to `0.0.0.0`.\n\n### Phase 2: Persistence Removal & Quarantine (High Priority)\n1. **Quarantine Dropper Binary & C2 Config**\n   - Action: Create secure directory `/var/quarantine/` (mode 700) and move malware files (`/disk/var/lib/pgsql/.local/pgdaemon:1`, `/disk/etc/pgdaemon.conf:3`).\n   - Command:\n     ```bash\n     mkdir -p /var/quarantine\n     chmod 700 /var/quarantine\n     cp -a /var/lib/pgsql/.local/pgdaemon /var/quarantine/pgdaemon.bak\n     cp -a /etc/pgdaemon.conf /var/quarantine/pgdaemon.conf.bak\n     rm -f /var/lib/pgsql/.local/pgdaemon /etc/pgdaemon.conf\n     ```\n   - Verification: `ls -la /var/lib/pgsql/.local/pgdaemon /etc/pgdaemon.conf` (confirm files no longer exist in original paths).\n\n2. **Disable Malicious Systemd Persistence Service**\n   - Action: Stop, disable, and quarantine `/etc/systemd/system/pg-metrics.service` (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/pg-metrics.service:5`). Do NOT touch `/etc/systemd/system/pg-backup.service` (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/pg-backup.service:3`).\n   - Command:\n     ```bash\n     systemctl stop pg-metrics.service\n     systemctl disable pg-metrics.service\n     mv /etc/systemd/system/pg-metrics.service /var/quarantine/\n     systemctl daemon-reload\n     ```\n   - Verification: `systemctl status pg-metrics.service` returns `Unit pg-metrics.service could not be found.`\n\n3. **Remediate Cron Persistence**\n   - Action: Backup and clean `/var/spool/cron/postgres` (`/disk/var/spool/cron/postgres:5`).\n   - Command:\n     ```bash\n     cp -a /var/spool/cron/postgres /var/quarantine/cron-postgres.bak\n     sed -i '/198\\.51\\.100\\.214/d' /var/spool/cron/postgres\n     ```\n   - Verification: `crontab -l -u postgres | grep 198.51.100.214` returns no matches.\n\n4. **Quarantine Timestomping Artifacts**\n   - Action: Move `/var/lib/pgsql/.local/.timestamps` (`/disk/var/lib/pgsql/.local/.timestamps:2`) to `/var/quarantine/`.\n   - Command: `mv /var/lib/pgsql/.local/.timestamps /var/quarantine/.timestamps.bak`\n   - Verification: Check `/var/lib/pgsql/.local/` to ensure hidden metadata file is removed.\n\n### Phase 3: Vulnerability Eradication & Hardening (Medium Priority)\n1. **PostgreSQL Authentication Hardening**\n   - Action: Update `/var/lib/pgsql/data/pg_hba.conf` (`/disk/var/lib/pgsql/data/pg_hba.conf:3`) to remove `trust` authentication and enforce password authentication (`scram-sha-256`) restricted to localhost or internal subnet.\n   - Command: Modify `/var/lib/pgsql/data/pg_hba.conf` and reload PostgreSQL (`systemctl reload postgresql`).\n   - Verification: Attempt connection without password from external host (connection refused/rejected).\n\n2. **PostgreSQL Privilege Control**\n   - Action: Revoke execution privileges on `COPY PROGRAM` from non-essential roles and set strong superuser password.\n   - Verification: `SELECT * FROM pg_user;` and audit superuser permissions.\n\n### Phase 4: Recovery & Monitoring (Ongoing)\n1. Deploy File Integrity Monitoring (FIM / `auditd`) on `/etc/systemd/system/` and `/var/spool/cron/`.\n2. Enable PostgreSQL connection logging and query auditing.\nEOF\n"] min_timeout_sec: 0.5 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
