Sending keys: ['python3 -c \'\nimport os\n\nvuln_report = """# Vulnerability-Driven Entry Analysis Report\n\n## Assessment Overview\nThis report analyzes whether software vulnerabilities (CVEs) contributed to the initial access or post-compromise progression on host `docker-prod-01`. Based on forensic evidence from `/disk` and security telemetry under `/sas`, **no software vulnerability was exploited**. The intrusion was enabled exclusively by architectural configuration weakness.\n\n---\n\n## Vulnerability Telemetry & Scan Analysis\n- **Vulnerability Feed**: The vulnerability scanning feed (`/sas/vulns.json:1`) returned an empty set (`[]`), confirming no active, unpatched CVEs were flagged by automated security controls.\n- **Change Ticket Discrepancy Reconciled**: Draft change ticket `CHG-1943` listed patching `CVE-2019-0708` (BlueKeep) on RDP (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:12`). Forensic analysis refutes this:\n  1. The host operating system is Ubuntu 22.04 LTS Linux (`/disk/etc/os-release:1`), whereas CVE-2019-0708 is a vulnerability specific to Microsoft Windows Remote Desktop Services (RDP).\n  2. No RDP service is present or active on the host (`/disk/etc/fstab:1`, `/disk/var/log/syslog:1`).\n\n---\n\n## Web Application Probe Analysis\nInspection of web server access logs (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log`) revealed external scanning activity from threat actor IP `198.51.100.102` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:8`):\n- **Webshell Upload Attempt**: `POST /uploads/shell.php` returning HTTP 200/814 bytes (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:379`).\n- **Log4Shell Attempt**: `GET /?x=jndi-ldap-lookup-defanged-to-198.51.100.102-1389` returning HTTP 500 (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:380`).\n- **Struts2 Probe**: `GET /struts2-showcase/` returning HTTP 200/308 bytes (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:381`).\n\nThese requests were unsuccessful automated exploitation probes (or defanged test vectors) and did not grant system access or code execution.\n\n---\n\n## Conclusion & Entry Vector Determination\nInitial access was achieved purely through **unauthenticated API exposure** rather than software vulnerability exploitation:\n- Docker Engine API was bound to all interfaces (`0.0.0.0:2375`) without TLS authentication (`/disk/etc/docker/daemon.json:19`, `/sas/baseline.json:3`).\n- This configuration allowed remote attacker `198.51.100.102` to issue unauthenticated REST requests directly to the Docker API (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:12`), launching a privileged container (`/disk/var/lib/docker/overlay2/attacker/diff/entrypoint.sh:4`) and escalating to root host access (`/disk/opt/xmrig/xmrig:1`).\n"""\n\nwith open("/app/vuln-report.md", "w") as f:\n    f.write(vuln_report)\n\nprint("vuln-report.md written.")\n\'\n'] min_timeout_sec: 0.5 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
