ling allows unauthenticated RDP protocol handshakes, enabling offline/online password brute-forcing directly against the Windows logon interface without requiring prior authentication.\n\n---\n\n## Summary Table\n\n| Category | Finding | CVE / Flaw ID | Confidence | Citation |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Software Vulnerabilities | None Identified | N/A | HIGH | `/sas/vulns.json:1` |\n| Proposed Remediation Row 2 | Incorrect BlueKeep claim | CVE-2019-0708 (Invalid) | HIGH | `/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:10`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:12` |\n| Primary Entry Vector | Weak Auth / Misconfiguration | N/A (T1110 Brute Force) | HIGH | `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg:4`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:12` |\nEOF\n"] min_timeout_sec: 0.5 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
