Sending keys: ["cat << 'EOF' > /app/vuln-report.md\n# Vulnerability Report: Entry Vector Analysis\n\n## 1. Primary Entry Vector Overview\nThe host `smb-prod-01` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6`) was compromised via remote exploitation of an unpatched SMBv1 service (`/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys`, `/sas/baseline.json:2`). The vulnerability leveraged by the attacker was **CVE-2017-0144** (MS17-010 / EternalBlue) (`/sas/vulns.json:3`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:16`).\n\n## 2. Vulnerability Details\n- **CVE Identifier**: CVE-2017-0144 (`/sas/vulns.json:3`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:16`)\n- **Severity Rating**: CVSS v3.1 Base Score 8.8 (HIGH) (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:16`)\n- **Vulnerability Class**: Remote Code Execution / Buffer Overflow in SMBv1 Server Driver\n- **Vulnerable Component**: `/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys` (`/sas/alerts.json:26`, `/sas/baseline.json:2`)\n- **Exploit Implant**: `/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe` (`/sas/alerts.json:2`, `/sas/vulns.json:3`)\n\n## 3. Technical Mechanism & Exploit Artifacts\nThe vulnerability resides in Microsoft Windows SMBv1 protocol processing within `srv.sys` (`/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys`). Remote unauthenticated attackers send specially crafted SMBv1 packets to port 445, triggering memory corruption in kernel space to execute arbitrary code. Upon successful exploitation, the DoublePulsar payload was injected, which dropped and executed the SMB exploit implant `mssecsvc.exe` located at `/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe` (`/sas/alerts.json:2`, `/sas/vulns.json:3`).\n\n## 4. Alternate Entry Vector Analysis\nAll other potential entry vectors (such as RDP / BlueKeep CVE-2019-0708 mentioned erroneously in initial tickets) were evaluated and ruled out based on disk and network evidence (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:8`, `/disk/inetpub/logs/LogFiles/W3SVC1/u_ex.log`). Web server logs (`/disk/inetpub/logs/LogFiles/W3SVC1/u_ex.log`) showed standard HTTP GET traffic without web exploitation attempts. The sole successful initial access vector was CVE-2017-0144 via SMBv1 (`/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys`, `/sas/vulns.json:3`).\nEOF\n"] min_timeout_sec: 0.5 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
