ows/System32/Tasks/UpdateHelper:2`), service `svc-helper` (`/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys:5`), and Run key `svc` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE:2`). |\n| 4 | Block malicious domains and quarantine payload binaries | C2: `update-rdp.example.cn`, Mining Pool: `xmr.rdp.evil`, Binary: `C:\\Users\\Public\\svc.exe` | PROPOSED | **ADDED**: Silent persistence items and IoCs missing from prior shift ticket (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:12`). Added Run key removal (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE:2`), binary quarantine (`/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe:1`), and C2/pool network blocking (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:23`, `/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys:9`). |\n\n---\n\n## Prioritised Remediation Steps & Verification\n\n### Phase 1: Immediate Network Isolation & Perimeter Blocking\n1. **Block Attacker IP & C2 Infrastructure**:\n   - Apply boundary firewall rule to drop inbound and outbound traffic to/from `198.51.100.92` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6`).\n   - Add DNS sinkhole / block rules for C2 domain `update-rdp.example.cn` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:23`, `/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys:9`) and mining pool host `xmr.rdp.evil` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:24`, `/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe:4`).\n   - **Verification**: Test DNS resolution and ping to `198.51.100.92` and verify dropped packets in firewall logs.\n\n2. **Isolate Compromised Host**:\n   - Isolate `rdp-prod-01` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`) from the local production VLAN while maintaining out-of-band management access for security responders.\n\n### Phase 2: RDP Hardening & Credential Protection\n1. **Enforce Network Level Authentication (NLA)**:\n   - Configure registry key `HKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Terminal Server\\WinStations\\RDP-Tcp`: set `UserAuthentication` to `1` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg:4`).\n   - Enforce via Group Policy Object (GPO): *Computer Configuration -> Administrative Templates -> Windows Components -> Remote Desktop Services -> Remote Desktop Session Host -> Security -> Require user authentication for remote connections by using Network Level Authentication*.\n   - **Verification**: Execute `Get-ItemProperty -Path \'HKLM:\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Terminal Server\\WinStations\\RDP-Tcp\' -Name UserAuthentication` and confirm value is `1`.\n\n2. **Credential Reset & Account Lockout Enforcement**:\n   - Reset passwords for all administrative accounts (including `Administrator` and `svc-backup`) (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security-events.csv:3`).\n   - Configure Account Lockout Policy (e.g. threshold = 5 failed attempts) to prevent brute-force attacks (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:12`).\n\n### Phase 3: Artifact Quarantine & Persistence Neutralization\nPer rules, artifacts must be **quarantined/backed up** rather than immediately deleted.\n\n1. **Quarantine Ransomware Payload (`C:\\Users\\Public\\svc.exe`)**:\n   - Action: Move `/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe` (`/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe:1`) to secure forensic quarantine folder `C:\\ProgramData\\Quarantine\\` and restrict ACLs.\n   - **Verification**: Confirm file is removed from `C:\\Users\\Public\\` and hashed.\n\n2. **Disable & Remove Scheduled Task (`UpdateHelper`)**:\n   - Action: Export task XML to quarantine backup, then run `schtasks /Change /TN "UpdateHelper" /Disable` and `schtasks /Delete /TN "UpdateHelper" /F` (`/disk/Windows/System32/Tasks/UpdateHelper:2`).\n   - **Verification**: Run `schtasks /Query /TN "UpdateHelper"` and confirm task is not found.\n\n3. **Disable & Quarantine Malicious Service (`svc-helper`)**:\n   - Action: Stop service `sc stop svc-helper`, set startup type to disabled `sc config svc-helper start= disabled`, backup service configuration, and move `/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys` (`/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys:1`) to quarantine. Delete service registry key `sc delete svc-helper`.\n   - **Verification**: Run `Get-Service -Name "svc-helper"` and confirm service is absent.\n\n4. **Remove Silent Registry