Sending keys: ["cat << 'EOF' > /app/intrusion-report.md\n# Post-Compromise Intrusion Investigation Report\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nAn external threat actor operating from source IP `198.51.100.167` compromised `struts-prod-01` through a multi-stage intrusion. Initial brute-force SSH attempts occurred on 2026-08-08 between 00:54:37 UTC and 00:56:00 UTC (`/disk/var/log/secure:182`), followed by web applications reconnaissance (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:391`). The attacker successfully exploited CVE-2023-50164, an OGNL injection vulnerability in Apache Struts2 (`/disk/opt/tomcat/lib/struts2-core.jar:1`, `/sas/alerts.json:27`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:13`).\n\nFollowing exploitation, the attacker dropped a JSP webshell (`/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp:1`), staged a database archive (`/disk/tmp/.cache/dump.tar.gz:1`), exfiltrated sensitive data via HTTPS/HTTP POST to `198.51.100.167` (`/disk/var/log/tomcat/access-exfil.log:116`), established persistent backdoors via SSH authorized_keys (`/disk/root/.ssh/authorized_keys:1`) and cron (`/disk/var/spool/cron/tomcat:5`), and attempted selective log wiping (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`).\n\n## Threat Entity Profile & Identifiers\n\n- **Attacker Source IP**: `198.51.100.167` (`/disk/var/log/secure:213`, `/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:391`, `/disk/var/log/tomcat/access-exfil.log:116`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:7`)\n- **Command & Control Domain**: `update-struts.example.cn` (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:19`)\n- **Mining Pool & Wallet (from persistent payload description)**:\n  - Pool: `stratum+tcp://xmr.struts.evil:3333` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:20`)\n  - Wallet: `4A000000000000000000e40b218944d0` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:21`)\n\n## Full Attack Chain & MITRE Enterprise ATT&CK Mapping\n\n### Step 1: Reconnaissance & Initial Access (T1190 - Exploit Public-Facing Application)\n- **Description**: The threat actor conducted SSH password brute-forcing (`/disk/var/log/secure:182`) gaining access (`/disk/var/log/secure:213`) and probed public endpoints (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:391`). The main web vector was Struts2 OGNL injection (CVE-2023-50164) targeting `/opt/tomcat/lib/struts2-core.jar` (`/disk/opt/tomcat/lib/struts2-core.jar:1`, `/sas/alerts.json:27`, `/sas/vulns.json:44`).\n- **ATT&CK Technique**: T1190 (Exploit Public-Facing Application) (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:9`)\n\n### Step 2: Persistence via Web Shell (T1505.003 - Web Shell)\n- **Description**: Upon gaining execution, the attacker dropped a JSP webshell at `/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp` (`/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp:1`, `/sas/alerts.json:1`).\n- **ATT&CK Technique**: T1505.003 (Web Shell) (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:10`)\n\n### Step 3: Command & Shell Execution (T1059.004 - Unix Shell)\n- **Description**: Arbitrary shell commands were executed via the webshell and local shell environments to inspect system resources and prepare staging scripts (`/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp:1`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:11`).\n- **ATT&CK Technique**: T1059.004 (Unix Shell) (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:11`)\n\n### Step 4: Data Collection & Staging (T1560.001 - Archive via Utility)\n- **Description**: Sensitive database content was dumped and staged as a tar archive disguised as `/tmp/.cache/dump.tar.gz` (`/disk/tmp/.cache/dump.tar.gz:1`, `/sas/alerts.json:10`).\n- **Note**: A separate file `/tmp/.cache/backup.tar.gz` (`/disk/tmp/.cache/backup.tar.gz:1`) was investigated and determined to be a benign scheduled maintenance job (`/disk/tmp/.cache/backup.tar.gz:1`).\n- **ATT&CK Technique**: T1560.001 (Archive via Utility) (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:12`)\n\n### Step 5: Data Exfiltration (T1048 - Exfiltration Over Alternative Protocol)\n- **Description**: Staged exfiltration data was transferred out of the network via HTTP/HTTPS POST requests to endpoint `198.51.100.167` (`/disk/var/log/tomcat/access-exfil.log:116`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:13`).\n- **Alert Status**: Silent at endpoint exfiltration destination; captured in web server traffic log (`/disk/var/log/tomcat/access-exfil.log:116`).\n- **ATT&CK Technique**: T1048 (Exfiltration Over Alternative Protocol) (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:13`)\n\n### Step 6: SSH Key Backdoor (T1098.004 - SSH Authorized Keys)\n- **Description**: The attacker inserted an unauthorized SSH public key into `/root/.ssh/authorized_keys` (`/disk/root/.ssh/authorized_keys:1`).\n- **Alert Status**: SILENT (Not present in SAS alert feed `/sas/alerts.json:1`).\n- **ATT&CK Technique**: T1098.004 (SSH Authorized Keys) (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:14`)\n\n### Step 7: Scheduled Job Persistence (T1053.003 - Cron)\n- **Description**: A malicious cron job was planted under the `tomcat` user cron spool at `/var/spool/cron/tomcat` (`/disk/var/spool/cron/tomcat:5`, `/sas/alerts.json:17`). The job periodic beacon fetches payloads from `http://198.51.100.167/x`.\n- **ATT&CK Technique**: T1053.003 (Cron) (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:15`)\n\n### Step 8: Defense Evasion & Anti-Forensics (T1070.002 - Clear Linux or Mac System Logs)\n- **Description**: The attacker executed selective log wiping routines targeting system authentication logs (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`).\n- **Alert Status**: SILENT (Not present in SAS alert feed `/sas/alerts.json:1`).\n- **ATT&CK Technique**: T1070.002 (Clear Linux or Mac System Logs) (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:16`)\n\n## Detection Coverage Analysis\n\n| ATT&CK Technique | Description | Artifact Path | SAS Alert Feed Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| T1190 | Struts2 Vulnerable Lib | `/opt/tomcat/lib/struts2-core.jar` | Covered (`/sas/alerts.json:27`) |\n| T1505.003 | JSP Webshell | `/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp` | Covered (`/sas/alerts.json:1`) |\n| T1560.001 | Staged Exfil Archive | `/tmp/.cache/dump.tar.gz` | Covered (`/sas/alerts.json:10`) |\n| T1048 | Data Exfiltration | `/var/log/tomcat/access-exfil.log` | Silent in SAS alert feed (`/disk/var/log/tomcat/access-exfil.log:116`) |