Sending keys: ["cat << 'EOF' > /app/vuln-report.md\n# Vulnerability-Driven Entry Analysis Report\n\n## 1. Vulnerability Assessment & Entry Vector Analysis\n\n### Confirmed Vulnerability: CVE-2023-50164 (Apache Struts2 File Upload Path Traversal / OGNL RCE)\n- **Vulnerability Identifier**: CVE-2023-50164 (`/sas/vulns.json:46`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:23`)\n- **CVSS Score**: 9.8 (CRITICAL) v3.1 (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:23`)\n- **CWE**: CWE-552 (Files or Directories Accessible to External Parties) (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:23`)\n- **Affected Component**: Apache Struts2 Core Library located at `/opt/tomcat/lib/struts2-core.jar` (`/disk/opt/tomcat/lib/struts2-core.jar:1`, `/sas/alerts.json:30`, `/sas/baseline.json:38`)\n- **Mechanism of Exploitation**: An attacker manipulates file upload parameter cases/paths during HTTP requests to enable path traversal. Under specific web application configurations, this allows uploading malicious files (such as JSP webshells) into web-accessible directories, resulting in Remote Code Execution (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:24`, `/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp:1`).\n- **Evidence of Exploitation**:\n  - Dropped JSP webshell at `/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp` (`/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp:1`, `/sas/alerts.json:6`, `/sas/vulns.json:47`).\n  - Web application logs showing HTTP POST and OGNL injection probes from IP `198.51.100.167` (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:391`).\n\n## 2. Rejection of Incorrect Vulnerability Claims\n\n### Erroneous Claim: CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep)\n- **Ticket Draft Entry**: Draft change ticket `CHG-7100` Row 2 suggests patching CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep) for RDP (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:59`).\n- **Evaluation**: CVE-2019-0708 is a vulnerability in Microsoft Remote Desktop Services (RDP). The target machine is a RHEL 9 Linux application server running Apache Struts2 on Apache Tomcat (`/disk/etc/os-release:1`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`). RDP is not installed or operational on this Linux host.\n- **Conclusion**: The BlueKeep claim is invalid and represents a misattribution by the previous shift. It must be rejected and replaced with remediation for CVE-2023-50164 (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:23`).\n\n## 3. Vulnerability Summary & Correlation Matrix\n\n| Identifier | Vulnerable Component | Vector / Technique | Citation |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| CVE-2023-50164 | `/opt/tomcat/lib/struts2-core.jar` | Path Traversal / OGNL Injection leading to JSP Webshell upload | `/disk/opt/tomcat/lib/struts2-core.jar:1`, `/sas/vulns.json:44`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:23` |\n| Weak SSH Credentials / Password Auth | `/etc/ssh/sshd_config` / `sshd` | SSH password brute-force allowed password authentication for root | `/disk/var/log/secure:182` |\n\nEOF\n"] min_timeout_sec: 0.5 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
