Sending keys: ["cat << 'EOF' > /app/baseline-report.md\n# Baseline and Configuration Weakness Report\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nA review of system configurations and baseline audit logs for `struts-prod-01` identified multiple critical security weaknesses. These baseline deficiencies enabled initial password brute-forcing, allowed web application exploitation, and permitted post-exploitation persistence and anti-forensics.\n\n## Baseline Audit Findings & Weaknesses\n\n### 1. Outdated and Vulnerable Software Components\n- **Finding**: Presence of vulnerable Struts2 library `/opt/tomcat/lib/struts2-core.jar` (`/disk/opt/tomcat/lib/struts2-core.jar:1`, `/sas/baseline.json:36`, `/sas/alerts.json:27`).\n- **Impact**: Allowed remote unauthenticated attacker to execute arbitrary code via OGNL injection (CVE-2023-50164) (`/sas/vulns.json:44`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:23`).\n\n### 2. Excessive Web Server Write Permissions & Static Directory Execution\n- **Finding**: Tomcat web application directory `/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/` allowed web server process write execution (`/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp:1`, `/sas/alerts.json:1`).\n- **Impact**: Allowed attacker to drop and execute JSP webshells directly within web-accessible static directory.\n\n### 3. Weak SSH Authentication & Direct Root SSH Login Enabled\n- **Finding**: SSH daemon configuration allowed password authentication and direct `root` login, facilitating SSH brute-force password spraying (`/disk/var/log/secure:182`).\n- **Impact**: Attacker successfully brute-forced root SSH password (`/disk/var/log/secure:213`) and subsequently appended persistent keys to `/root/.ssh/authorized_keys` (`/disk/root/.ssh/authorized_keys:1`).\n\n### 4. Unmonitored Cron Job Permissions and Spool Security\n- **Finding**: Lack of strict access control and auditing on user cron spools (`/var/spool/cron/tomcat`) (`/disk/var/spool/cron/tomcat:1`, `/sas/alerts.json:17`).\n- **Impact**: Allowed unprivileged web service accounts to create background persistent tasks beaconing to malicious external IPs (`/disk/var/spool/cron/tomcat:5`).\n\n### 5. Inadequate Audit Logging and Log Protection\n- **Finding**: Local logs were susceptible to unauthorized tampering and deletion without offsite syslog/SIEM forwarding (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`).\n- **Impact**: Threat actor selectively wiped authentication logs to hinder forensic investigation (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`).\n\n## Baseline Findings Matrix\n\n| Baseline Check ID | Weakness Description | Location / Path | Status | Citation |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| CHK-05 / BAS-01 | Outdated Struts2 Core Library | `/opt/tomcat/lib/struts2-core.jar` | NON-COMPLIANT | `/disk/opt/tomcat/lib/struts2-core.jar:1`, `/sas/baseline.json:36` |\n| CHK-01 | Writable Web Root Directory | `/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/` | NON-COMPLIANT | `/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp:1` |\n| CHK-04 | Unmonitored User Cron Spool | `/var/spool/cron/tomcat` | NON-COMPLIANT | `/disk/var/spool/cron/tomcat:1` |\n| SSH-BASE-01 | Password Auth & Root Login | `/etc/ssh/sshd_config` / `sshd` | NON-COMPLIANT | `/disk/var/log/secure:182` |\n\nEOF\n"] min_timeout_sec: 0.5 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
